      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Queensland%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "To the north, Maryland Route 4 borders Queensland; U.S. 301 lies to the south and east, while Marlboro Pike and South Osborne Road run west.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Queensland%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Queensland shares borders with Westphalia, Marlboro Village, and Brock Hall to the north, Croom southeast, Marlton south, and Rosaryville southwest.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Queensland%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Residents fall under Marlton Elementary and Melwood Elementary for primary education, and James Madison Middle School for middle grades.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Queensland%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
